ystem \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 6.5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{aligned}]}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 15\\end{aligned}]}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ is the parameter vector, and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector.\n\nThus, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072540/assets/b5302251a49a45514a55d2987289548e2a55917884ff4c240be081ba512a970e.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072540/example-5614.json" "file_sha256" "1bb99f85f9202a603531a5c6ace405acb62d3c80d577941b1ad004455d25129b"} {"question" "e-5615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "| $x_1$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x_2$ | **$-8$** | **$-2$** | **$6$** | **$15$** |\n| $x_3$ | **$8$** | **$6$** | **$4$** | **$2$** |\n| $y$ | $10$ | $20$ | $40$ | $60$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the hyperplane $y = \\beta_1 x_1 + \\beta_2 x_2 +\\beta_3 x_3$ that best fits the data above can be found using multiple linear regression as \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072540/assets/3f86f03e3a32ede2ac18d6c39f62de5686a74d4050b8c1d7aa2a6fc3e2cdddbb.png)\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector. Find  $X$ and $\\mathbf{y}$ in this context." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072540/example-5615.json" "file_sha256" "4799b52de95ffe08849f1b5724a359f470f6bd14c9348224bdfd5d4299c9935c"} {"question" "e-5615" 